090 nemotron-moe-serial-path: env switch to run the NemotronH shared + routed experts serially

On CUDA NemotronHMoE always takes _forward_core_shared_routed_overlap: the routed experts launch on
an alternate stream while the shared expert runs on the main stream. At TP=2 on GA102 with the
INT4 routed kernel (fused_moe_kernel_gptq_awq) and the shared expert on the AWQ dequantize + cuBLAS
path, the concurrent launch stretches the routed gate/up kernel from 124 us to 124 + k x 37 us
(k = 0..6, per token, uncorrelated across ranks) - 3.3..5.0 ms of an 11 ms decode step.
SGLANG_NEMOTRON_MOE_STREAM_OVERLAP=0 takes _forward_core_normal instead (same math, one stream).
nemotron3-omni tripwire, two interleaved boots per arm: 91.5 / 93.8 / 89.8 and 92.4 / 94.9 / 89.6
-> 115.9 / 114.9 / 107.0 and 116.3 / 114.7 / 106.8 tok/s at 1K / 32K / 262K.
Default (unset or 1) keeps upstream behaviour.
---
diff --git a/python/sglang/srt/models/nemotron_h.py b/python/sglang/srt/models/nemotron_h.py
index 0d88bb4312..b7d5620b3b 100644
--- a/python/sglang/srt/models/nemotron_h.py
+++ b/python/sglang/srt/models/nemotron_h.py
@@ -152,6 +152,9 @@ class NemotronHMLP(nn.Module):
         return x
 
 
+import os as _os
+
+_MOE_STREAM_OVERLAP = _os.environ.get("SGLANG_NEMOTRON_MOE_STREAM_OVERLAP", "1") != "0"
 _alt_stream = None
 
 
@@ -374,7 +377,7 @@ class NemotronHMoE(nn.Module):
             and is_sm120()
         ):
             return self._forward_core_prefill_overlap(hidden_states)
-        if _is_cuda and (
+        if _is_cuda and _MOE_STREAM_OVERLAP and (
             not get_moe_a2a_backend().is_flashinfer() or get_is_capture_mode()
         ):
             return self._forward_core_shared_routed_overlap(hidden_states)
